.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Landmarks derived from third-party footage. Kept out of the repo because the source
# videos carry their own licenses; see temporal/SOURCES.md for how to regenerate it.
temporal/external_clips.npz

# Your own recordings and the models trained from them ARE meant to be committed --
# collect_motion.py stores landmarks rather than JPEGs precisely so that stays cheap
# (a few hundred KB, against the 650 MB of images in RandomForest/data).

# Generated by docs/export_models.py alongside models.json; GitHub Pages compresses
# on the fly, so only the plain .json is served. Kept local for the gzip test.
docs/models.json.gz

# Diagnostics the local dev server writes when the page posts to /log.
docs/browser_log.jsonl

# Written by docs/make_demo.sh beside the committed GIF. It is the asset to drag into a
# GitHub editor for an inline player; the repo itself ships the GIF.
docs/demo.mp4
